      "content": "While tea tree oil may have some antiseptic properties, its effectiveness is debated, and it's not a substitute for proper treatment. Overusing tea tree oil can lead to skin irritation and even allergic reactions. As for keeping the skin moist, you're right that applying a moisturizer can help. However, considering your burn is still pulsing and warm to the touch, delay applying any topical treatments until the burn has cooled down and reached normal temperature. In the meantime, continue to keep the area clean and cool, and see a healthcare professional if the burn shows signs of infection, such as redness, swelling, or pus.",
